{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1363003-2e-are-conditions-in-scion","id":1363003,"title":"[2E] Are Conditions in Scion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-23T20:54:05-08:00","id":1363003,"title":"[2E] Are Conditions in Scion?","content":"On this, I <i>know</i> there are Conditions in <b>Scion</b> 2E. I only get the topic name from my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278246-2e-are-there-merits-in-scion\">previous topic on mechanics of gameline</a>, comparing them to Merits. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The question I want to rise here is more precisely '<i><b>where</b></i> are Conditions in <b>Scion</b> 2E'? I know there are general rules for them in <b>Scion: Origin</b> book, page 66, but I cannot mark where are exemplary Conditions for the gameline.<br /> <br /> As old <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> Storyteller I'm accustom to Appendix with whole Conditions lists - and in <b>Scion</b> I do not seem to have in both <b>Origin</b> and <b>Hero</b> books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, I read it correctly that <i>Persistent Conditions</i> are characters Flaws that generate Momentum in session gameplay? And <i>Fields</i> are similar to idea of Framing Scenes from <b>Hurt Locker</b> book of <b>CoD</b>?<br /> <br /> If yes on Persistent Conditions, it's weird there is no Conditions section on the official char sheet for the game ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-23-2020, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T01:01:11-08:00","id":1363035,"title":"","content":"Well for one, injuries are a kind of condition, so take a note on that.<br /> <br /> The very nature of Conditions means that the only 'designated space' that would be the right size would be 'The backside of the character sheet'. That's an unfortunate tendency with WW/OPP character sheets. They're never big enough. I recommend a pack of index cards, just in general.<br /> <br /> See, the thing as to why there's no big list of Conditions is that it would suggest that there's a limit to them, while Conditions are basically any kind of Thing that a character is under.<br /> <br /> Why isn't there a standardized list? Because if you make a &quot;Blind: +3 difficulty to rolls that require sight&quot;, then players won't realize that there are degrees to the Conditions. So Blindness can be:<ul><li>Sand In The Eyes: +1 Difficulty to attack rolls. Resolved by taking an action to flush the eyes with water or rub them.</li> <li>Blinded by the Light: +3 to Difficulty to rolls that require sight. Resolved at the end of the scene, or through healing magic.</li> <li>Eyes Dissolved: Any actions entirely dependent on sight are impossible. Resolved through divine healing magic.</li> </ul><br /> See, there's no &quot;Standard&quot; list of effects. There are some Conditions here and there, but word space was at a premium, so I understand why they didn't put an appendix in the book. If I get an idea I may make a Big List of Conditions.<br /> <br /> As for Fields, they're like Conditions that apply to the entire scene. A shattering earthquake tearing the ground asunder, a thunderstorm unleashing rain and lightning upon the world, a biting sandstorm, those are examples of Field effects.<br /> <br /> (Also, this seemed most relevant here, but you don't need to update your Hub Post every time you ask a question. If you use it for your collection of actual homebrew stuff, whatever, but &quot;I had a question that got answered&quot; is not worth adding to your Index Of Posts Made)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T05:08:11-08:00","id":1363057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1363003-2e-are-conditions-in-scion?p=1363035#post1363035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The very nature of Conditions means that the only 'designated space' that would be the right size would be 'The backside of the character sheet'. That's an unfortunate tendency with WW/OPP character sheets. They're never big enough. I recommend a pack of index cards, just in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you do not seen <b>CoD</b> sheets and how we limited Condition in those only to small frame for it, having reference in corebooks. I know this, as I designed most fan sheets for Ephemeral Entities, <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>WtF</b> 2E, <b>BtP</b> 2E and many, many more - all to be seen on <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Mr. Gone site</a>, as fan variants. Why not simple frame could be put on <b>Scion</b> sheets?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1363003-2e-are-conditions-in-scion?p=1363035#post1363035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the thing as to why there's no big list of Conditions is that it would suggest that there's a limit to them, while Conditions are basically any kind of Thing that a character is under.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird, in <b>CoD</b> books we have ready lists and still play that we can invent new ones, on fly. Strange... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T11:19:57-08:00","id":1363146,"title":"","content":"A list of conditions and associated mechanics could make for a nice project for the nexus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The thing about having it in the core books is that personnaly, while i wouldnt have complained at seeing a list, there is nothing i wouldve cut from the current core books to feature a list of conditions instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T11:24:43-08:00","id":1363150,"title":"","content":"Indeed there is already a list of conditions for Trinity in the Nexus. I didn\u2019t buy it yet, but probably going to work for Scion too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T11:33:53-08:00","id":1363152,"title":"","content":"Oooh, a potential project for the nexus could feature 2 sections.<br /> One for injury conditions and another for curses.<br /> The document could also not just list the conditions mechanically but talk about how injuries and curses are presented myths and legends.<br /> <br /> Such a product would be a definite buy from me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T15:46:37-08:00","id":1363210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1363003-2e-are-conditions-in-scion?p=1363057#post1363057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird, in <b>CoD</b> books we have ready lists and still play that we can invent new ones, on fly. Strange... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>See my face?<br /> <br /> :|<br /> <br /> That encompasses how little I care about anything CoD related. I don't want it anywhere near my Scion, thank you kindly.<br /> <br /> Edit: Now again, a list of conditions wouldn't be a bad thing, but I can't think of anything in the books I'd cut to make room for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T22:47:44-08:00","id":1363255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1363003-2e-are-conditions-in-scion?p=1363210#post1363210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: Now again, a list of conditions wouldn't be a bad thing, but I can't think of anything in the books I'd cut to make room for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh Wordcount, she be a cruel mistress.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T06:44:17-08:00","id":1363956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1363003-2e-are-conditions-in-scion?p=1363057#post1363057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird, in <b>CoD</b> books we have ready lists and still play that we can invent new ones, on fly. Strange... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's because in CoD they often need to explain some of the more unique conditions, like when someone is acting under discreat or the incredibly stupid Abruption condition.<br /> Scionwise condistions are a lot more simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23543-penguinbowler","name":"Penguinbowler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T06:44:17-08:00","id":136